---
import { readFile } from 'node:fs/promises';
import BackroadPage from '../store-shell/BackroadPage.astro';
interface Props { view?: 'overview' | 'history' | 'contributions' }
const { view = 'overview' } = Astro.props;
const overview = view === 'overview';
const title = overview ? 'The experiment' : view === 'history' ? 'Build history' : 'DinkusKit contributions';
let status: any = null;
if (overview) {
  try { status = JSON.parse(await readFile('/var/lib/backroadbum/telemetry.json','utf8')); } catch {}
}
const show = (value: unknown, suffix = '') => value === null || value === undefined ? 'Unavailable' : `${value}${suffix}`;
const stale = status ? Date.now() - Date.parse(status.collectedAt) > 180000 : true;
const activity = status?.activity?.schema === 'backroadbum.activity/v1' ? status.activity : null;
const checkoutHistory = status?.checkoutHistory?.schema === 'backroadbum.checkout-observations/v1' ? status.checkoutHistory : null;
const checkoutProbe = status?.checkoutProbe?.schema === 'backroadbum.checkout-probe/v1' ? status.checkoutProbe : null;
const probeLabels = new Map<string, string>([
  ['ready-advisory', 'Test readiness supported'], ['admission-closed', 'Admission deliberately closed'],
  ['readiness-unavailable', 'Readiness advisory unavailable'], ['timeout', 'Probe timed out'],
  ['network-error', 'Network request failed'], ['invalid-json', 'Response was not valid JSON'],
  ['body-too-large', 'Response exceeded the probe limit'], ['contract-rejected', 'Response contract not recognized'],
  ['read-error', 'Response could not be read'], ['probe-error', 'Probe could not complete'],
]);
const checkoutWindows = checkoutHistory ? [...(checkoutHistory.active ? [checkoutHistory.active] : []), ...checkoutHistory.recent] : [];
const observationTime = (value: string) => new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-US', { year: 'numeric', month: 'short', day: 'numeric', hour: '2-digit', minute: '2-digit', second: '2-digit', hour12: false, timeZone: 'UTC', timeZoneName: 'short' }).format(new Date(value));
const numeric = (value: unknown, digits = 0) => typeof value === 'number' && Number.isFinite(value) ? new Intl.NumberFormat('en-US', { maximumFractionDigits: digits }).format(value) : 'Unavailable';
const minutes = (value: unknown) => typeof value === 'number' && Number.isFinite(value) ? `${numeric(value / 60, 1)} min` : 'Unavailable';
const dollars = (value: unknown) => typeof value === 'number' && Number.isFinite(value) ? new Intl.NumberFormat('en-US', { style: 'currency', currency: 'USD' }).format(value) : 'Unavailable';
---
<BackroadPage title={title} description="A public record of building and operating Backroad Bum with EmDash and DinkusKit.">
<section class="brb-page dashboard" data-dashboard-view={view}>
  <h1>{overview ? 'A store, built in the open.' : title}</h1>
  <p class="lead">{overview ? 'Backroad Bum is a working merchant experiment for EmDash and DinkusKit. This is the record of what is deployed, what is still missing and what running it teaches us.' : view === 'history' ? 'The dated record, newest first. Earlier observations stay intact; the overview reports the current serving state.' : 'Store-discovered friction, fork candidates and upstream reviews. Passing checks are not a release or a shared-service deployment.'}</p>
  <nav class="dashboard-nav" aria-label="Dashboard pages"><a href="/dashboard/" aria-current={overview ? 'page' : undefined}>Overview</a><a href="/dashboard/history/" aria-current={view === 'history' ? 'page' : undefined}>Build history</a><a href="/dashboard/contributions/" aria-current={view === 'contributions' ? 'page' : undefined}>Contributions</a></nav>
  {overview && <>
  <nav class="dashboard-nav dashboard-sections" aria-label="Dashboard sections"><a href="#current">Current state</a><a href="#history">Latest work</a><a href="#contributions">Open reviews</a><a href="#emdash-bugs">EmDash review</a><a href="#costs">Activity & costs</a><a href="#instructions">Instructions</a></nav>
  <section id="current"><h2>Current state</h2><p><strong>Owner Steer 1:</strong> connect through the real hosted DinkusKit customer flow with unmodified Registry plugins. The redundant local Payments and practice Ship services are now stopped and disabled; signed plugins use the hosted platform. The cart fix is open as PR #212; desktop, phone and Registry CI checks have passed. A fresh hosted Stripe TEST payment, paid receipt and sandbox fulfillment are now proven; public demo checkout is open again.</p><p>Six EmDash-backed product families, including a three-size tee and a bandana, two collections, a persistent guest cart and five field notes, with Commerce-owned pricing. Signed Registry Commerce 0.8.0, Payments 0.5.0 and Ship 0.3.1 are installed, with the catalog and order history preserved. Commerce, Payments and Ship are connected to hosted DinkusKit. TEST checkout settings now use $5 shipping, free from $75; the native refresh restored retained receipts. Fresh native Payments checks now report TEST readiness, superseding the earlier CAPTCHA snapshot. A shopper paid $21 for a bandana and shipping through the private same-origin preview; Payments confirms the provider payment and canonical TEST order #1006. Native Ship bought one free USPS sandbox label, its PDF reprints identically, and Commerce recorded matching completion and tracking. Public TEST checkout reopened after that proof; account email remains independently paused. Checkout request limits remain durable and health checks create no checkout capability.</p>
    <dl class="status-list">
      <div><dt>Store process</dt><dd>{show(status?.services?.backroadbum)}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>HTTPS proxy</dt><dd>{show(status?.services?.caddy)}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Local Payments · retired</dt><dd>{show(status?.services?.['backroadbum-payments'])} · disabled at retirement</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Local practice Ship · retired</dt><dd>{show(status?.services?.['backroadbum-ship'])} · disabled at retirement</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Historical local Ship proof</dt><dd>Authenticated packing setup · not hosted fulfillment</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Old Stripe TEST webhook</dt><dd>Disabled November 10 · endpoint retained, not deleted</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Former local API routes</dt><dd>Closed with HTTP 404 · hosted Connect proof routes remain public</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Admin boundary</dt><dd>{status?.http?.['/_emdash/admin'] === 401 ? 'Authenticated access required (HTTP 401)' : 'Unavailable — check required'}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Shopper API boundary</dt><dd>{status?.shopperAccounts?.state === 'capability-required' ? 'Commerce requires a shopper session' : status?.shopperAccounts?.state === 'blocked-by-admin-auth' ? 'Blocked by merchant authentication — check required' : 'Unavailable'}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Email sign-in</dt><dd>Paused · email delivery is unavailable; browser-bound receipts still work</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Hosted test checkout</dt><dd>Provider payment, Commerce receipt and sandbox fulfillment verified</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Closed-tab recovery</dt><dd>TEST Order #1007 saved by the background task before a post-payment receipt check · receipt recovered · no new label</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Address correction</dt><dd>Order #1007 corrected and restored · hosted Ship synchronized · stale save refused · still unlabelled</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Variant packing</dt><dd>TEST order #1008 paid $73 for M/L tees and shipping · address corrected through Commerce · one USPS sandbox label/PDF and matching completion verified · frozen choices intact · native Orders and Ship still omit sizes · <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/commerce/pull/263">PR #263</a> addresses Orders only; <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/commerce/issues/264">#264 tracks Ship’s missing choices</a></dd></div>
      <div><dt>Native package weight</dt><dd>Missing item weights appear as 0 oz without a warning in signed Ship · <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/ship/pull/97">PR #97</a> marks the total incomplete and asks for a weighed package · locally verified, not released</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Hosted shipping threshold</dt><dd>$74 basket + $5 shipping; $76 basket ships free · Commerce and Stripe agree · unpaid sessions only</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Checkout review</dt><dd>Phone order summary before contact entry · desktop summary stays on the right · one editable Commerce view</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Contact corrections</dt><dd>Local errors stay beside contact fields and receive focus after an invalid submission · editing clears them without moving focus · <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/template-store/pull/223">PR #223</a> proposes the generic fix</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Product identifiers</dt><dd>Selected sizes never borrow the default size’s SKU, GTIN or MPN · missing member identifiers are omitted · simple-product identifiers stay visible</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Product pictures</dt><dd>Bandana’s original image plus a native Commerce detail view · keyboard selection and no-JavaScript image links</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Editorial</dt><dd>Five EmDash field notes · latest: <a href="/field-note-before-the-signal-drops">Before the signal drops</a> · native ordered list, inline links and draft privacy verified</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Native availability</dt><dd>Tote available on backorder at $32 · saved in Commerce · visible through checkout review without an invented dispatch date</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Native pricing</dt><dd>Bandana Sale $14, Regular $16 in Commerce · current shopping views show $14 · existing paid receipt keeps its $16 line</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Unpaid recovery</dt><dd>Three original attempts still pending after their payment windows · <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/payments/issues/118">Payments #118 investigates recovery</a> · cause and safe next action unconfirmed</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Payment-page size labels</dt><dd>M and L remain distinct in Commerce but look identical in Stripe · reported as Commerce #262</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Collection discovery</dt><dd>Homepage links to Road day and Slow camp · published EmDash copy · current Commerce products</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Collection merchandising</dt><dd>Native published product order · Road day leads with the bandana and keeps the backordered tote last · saved drafts stay private</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Shopper flow</dt><dd>Public TEST checkout open · email sign-in remains paused</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Public admission</dt><dd>{show(status?.checkout?.admission)} · {show(status?.checkout?.state)}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Fulfillment</dt><dd>Hosted USPS sandbox label printed · canonical TEST completion · no live carrier scans</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Non-creating checkout probe</dt><dd>{show(status?.checkout?.healthHttp, ' HTTP')}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Latest probe result / elapsed time</dt><dd data-checkout-probe>{probeLabels.get(checkoutProbe?.outcome) ?? 'Unavailable'} · {numeric(checkoutProbe?.elapsedMs)} ms</dd></div>
      <div><dt>CPU sample</dt><dd>{show(status?.host?.cpuPercent, '%')}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Memory used / total</dt><dd>{show(status?.host?.usedMiB)} / {show(status?.host?.totalMiB)} MiB</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Swap used</dt><dd>{show(status?.host?.swapUsedMiB, ' MiB')}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Disk used / total</dt><dd>{show(status?.host?.diskUsedGiB)} / {show(status?.host?.diskTotalGiB)} GiB</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Last local backup</dt><dd>{show(status?.backupAt)}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Recovery coverage</dt><dd>Content/uploads plus the EmDash encryption key · encrypted settings recovered locally · retired Payments/Ship data retained · full runtime and off-host recovery unverified</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Visitor / order aggregates</dt><dd>Unavailable · counting is not wired yet</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <p class="small">Metrics refresh independently every minute. Last sample: {show(status?.collectedAt)}{stale ? ' · stale or unavailable' : ''}. Readiness is an advisory, not proof of payment. Retired-service data remains in private local recovery; it is not hosted fulfillment.</p>
    <section data-checkout-history aria-labelledby="checkout-observations-title">
      <h3 id="checkout-observations-title">Checkout readiness history</h3>
      {checkoutHistory ? <>
        <p>Monitoring began <time datetime={checkoutHistory.since}>{observationTime(checkoutHistory.since)}</time>. The latest five unavailable windows are retained, plus any open window. These are sampled observations, not continuous uptime or payment outcomes.</p>
        {checkoutWindows.length === 0 ? <p>No unavailable observations have been recorded since monitoring began. Earlier history is not backfilled.</p> : <ol>{checkoutWindows.map(window => <li>
          <p>Unavailable observed <time datetime={window.firstObservedAt}>{observationTime(window.firstObservedAt)}</time> through <time datetime={window.lastObservedAt}>{observationTime(window.lastObservedAt)}</time>: {window.unavailableSamples} unavailable {window.unavailableSamples === 1 ? 'sample' : 'samples'}; last HTTP {window.lastHttp ?? 'unavailable'}.
          {window.endingState ? <> Next observed: {window.endingState === 'ready-advisory' ? 'test readiness supported' : 'admission closed, not a readiness recovery'} at <time datetime={window.endedAt}>{observationTime(window.endedAt)}</time>.</> : <> Unavailable at the last sample.</>}</p>
        </li>)}</ol>}
        {checkoutHistory.lastGap && <p>Last gap between retained samples: <time datetime={checkoutHistory.lastGap.after}>{observationTime(checkoutHistory.lastGap.after)}</time> and <time datetime={checkoutHistory.lastGap.before}>{observationTime(checkoutHistory.lastGap.before)}</time>. The state in between is unknown.</p>}
      </> : <p>Unavailable — no readable observation history. Missing history is not zero failures.</p>}
    </section>
  </section>
  <section id="history"><h2>Latest work</h2><p>Local backups contained encrypted EmDash connection settings but omitted their decryption key. New private archives retain the matching key, and an offline temporary restore successfully decrypted all three stored connection settings without network access or replacing live files. This is credential recovery, not a full store restart or off-host disaster-recovery proof.</p><p><a href="/dashboard/history/">Read the full build history</a></p></section>
  <section id="contributions"><h2>Open reviews</h2><p>Seventeen fork PRs are open. Template PR #226 proposes the truthful return-page initial state; local unit/workflow, Registry and eight targeted desktop/phone cases pass, and full GitHub desktop, phone and aggregate checks now pass at 6f8106c; maintainer review is pending. Commerce PR #266 proposes the native order-list chronology repair with complete local checks, targeted installed proof and passing full GitHub CI at da754ae; maintainer review is pending. DinkusKit PR #124 now has passing full GitHub verification as well as complete local stage-by-stage checks; maintainer review is pending. Ship PR #97 passes full local verification and six native desktop/phone rendering cases; its substantive CI awaits maintainer approval, as do Ship’s two earlier repairs. Commerce PR #263 and template PR #225 have passing full GitHub checks; PR #223 remains queued without jobs. Checks are separate from review, signed release and shared deployment.</p><p><a href="/dashboard/contributions/">Open the contribution ledger</a></p></section>
  </>}
  {view === 'history' && <section id="history"><h2>Cycle entries</h2><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 12, 2026 · Recovering encrypted connections</h3><p>Earlier local snapshots contained encrypted plugin settings without their decryption key. The snapshot writer now includes only the allowlisted key ring, checks matching key coverage and refuses a rotation during copying; an offline restore decrypted all three connection settings and correctly refused an older keyless archive. Synthetic tests cover unsafe extraction, missing and incorrect keys, ciphertext corruption and retention; live settings and all eight Orders stayed unchanged. Full runtime and off-host recovery remain unverified.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 12, 2026 · Safer test contact details</h3><p>The shopper guides still recommended invented streets after a sandbox carrier had refused one. Native EmDash edits now offer an invented name, reserved example email and a public address fixture used successfully in testing; they distinguish label refusal from payment failure and explain merchant address correction. Draft isolation, native publication and desktop/phone/no-JavaScript reading pass, with seven other pages, the catalog and all eight Orders unchanged; no payment or label was created.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 12, 2026 · Before the receipt check starts</h3><p>Without JavaScript, the last-checkout page stayed on “Checking the saved checkout status” even though no check was running. Its initial heading and message now describe an unchecked state, explain JavaScript/reload and preserve the original browser’s site data; normal receipt and retry logic are unchanged. Template PR #226 proposes the same small repair, with unit/workflow, Registry and eight targeted desktop/phone cases passing; the inherited full local admin timeout is disclosed rather than called a passing matrix.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 12, 2026 · Explaining probe failures</h3><p>Two retained checkout-health samples had no usable response, but the collector discarded the error. Its single non-creating request now distinguishes timeout, network, response and contract failures, records elapsed time and keeps known HTTP status even when the body is unreadable. Actual unavailable samples leave a sanitized operator journal event; no raw bodies or exception messages are retained, and the earlier cause remains unknown.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 12, 2026 · Packing the two-size order</h3><p>Native Ship quoted the existing order #1008, but the sandbox provider refused its fictional destination before making a label. Commerce’s Correct address form saved a public test address already accepted on order #1006; Ship received the correction, then one USPS Ground Advantage sandbox label succeeded at a demo whole-package weight of 16.5 oz. The normal background task recorded matching Commerce completion, and an existing-label PDF read returned identical bytes without another purchase. Frozen payment and size choices remain unchanged; the separate missing-size handoff report and all sixteen PR reviews remain open.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 12, 2026 · Choosing a tee size</h3><p>The size selector worked, but shoppers had no measurements to compare M and L. EmDash’s native section and specification-table controls now hold measuring instructions and clearly illustrative M/L/XL dimensions; a normal keyboard link leads there from the introduction. Native save, reload, keyboard reordering and draft isolation were checked before publication. No price, stock, size identity, order or payment rule changed, and all sixteen upstream candidates remain open for review.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 12, 2026 · Retaining readiness observations</h3><p>The last cycle’s temporary 503 exposed a gap: minute telemetry replaced the evidence as soon as readiness recovered. The independent collector now retains a bounded, private observation history, with public-safe timestamps, sample counts, explicit gaps and separate planned-closure outcomes. Eighteen focused tests cover the recorder and existing probe boundaries; no historical windows are invented or checkout rules changed.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 12, 2026 · Recent payments first</h3><p><a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/commerce/pull/266">Commerce PR #266</a> proposes native Orders sorted by recorded payment time before pagination, with deterministic legacy and tie fallback. All 850 unit/workflow tests, 111 integrations, typecheck, Registry checks and installed desktop/phone pagination and keyboard proof pass locally. The candidate leaves storage/API order, numbering, frozen records and fulfillment unchanged; full GitHub CI now passes at da754ae, and no signed store plugin was replaced. Checkout’s advisory returned 503 after restart and recovered at its normal 08:47 UTC cache expiry; no cache or payment state was reset.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 12, 2026 · Finding the latest order</h3><p>The native Orders list placed the newest paid order fifth, requiring a phone scroll past older orders. A clean upstream replay confirms internal-ID sorting can push the latest payment onto a later page; <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/commerce/issues/265">Commerce #265</a> reports the chronology gap separately from order-scan performance. Inspect and Back still identify the exact order, and all Orders, numbering and catalog records remain unchanged; no repair is deployed.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 12, 2026 · Easier navigation targets</h3><p>Main and footer links now have at least 48×48px tap areas, replacing the footer’s roughly 23px-high anchors with clickable padding. The existing labels, routes and visual language stay intact; keyboard destinations, no-JavaScript browsing and real enlarged-font reflow are verified. No catalog, order, label or checkout setting changed, and no new upstream item was opened.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 12, 2026 · Before the signal drops</h3><p>Published a fifth field note through EmDash’s native editor, including a four-item numbered list and two inline links to related reading. Draft privacy, saved revision read-back, public search and same-tab keyboard navigation are verified; the eight earlier pages and Commerce records remain unchanged. Reading lists now have breathing room and inline links inherit the store’s ink, underline and focus treatment. DinkusKit PR #124’s full CI passed; no new upstream item or shared deployment is claimed.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 12, 2026 · Shipping settings ready for review</h3><p>Completed the hosted checkout-form candidate’s remaining verification and opened <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/dinkuskit/pull/124">DinkusKit PR #124</a>. All check stages pass across serial runs after repairing an older workflow matcher for Astro’s scoped attributes; native desktop/phone form checks also pass. The patch addresses the field collision in #123, not its wider dashboard redesign, and is not deployed to the shared service.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 12, 2026 · One shipping field at a time</h3><p>Hosted Commerce setup puts the flat shipping amount beside the free-shipping threshold label on desktop and phone, the same collision already tracked in <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/dinkuskit/issues/123">DinkusKit #123</a>. Prepared a focused layout candidate with passing desktop/phone, light/dark and native invalid-form checks. Full qualification remains unfinished after a separate local Inventory workflow failed, so no PR, full-suite pass or shared deployment is claimed. Hosted settings, catalog and Orders were not edited.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 12, 2026 · A checkout check you can retry</h3><p>The automatic availability check hid the store’s request-limit explanation and left no retry action. Cart and checkout now distinguish a limited check from an unavailable one and offer Check checkout availability without reloading contact or quantity drafts. This merchant repair preserves server limits and active-checkout recovery; it creates no payment, order or label.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 12, 2026 · Keep your place in the cart</h3><p>Removing the middle of three items with the keyboard sent focus back to the first row. Cart and checkout now move to the next surviving item’s quantity, or the nearest previous item when removing the last row; removing the final item keeps the existing empty-state focus. Quantity corrections and focus survive the following Commerce refresh, with no new payment, order or label.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 12, 2026 · Keep the sizes through packing</h3><p>Confirmed that native and hosted Ship show two identical tee lines while Commerce still retains the paid M/L choices. <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/commerce/issues/264">Commerce #264</a> records the sender/receiver gap and already-synced-order question, with a synthetic replay against untouched upstream source; no new wire contract or implementation is claimed. Archived Owner Steer 2 and cleared leftover generated files and dependency links from idle Ship worktrees; catalog, Orders and hosted settings are unchanged.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 12, 2026 · The size you picked, not its sibling</h3><p>Choosing L on the tee still showed M’s SKU, even though its cart identity and price were correct. The theme now shows only the selected option’s public SKU and omits absent member identifiers; simple products keep their own identifiers, and default GTIN/MPN never leak into a selected size. Desktop, phone and no-JavaScript checks preserve prices, stock and stale-option recovery; this merchant repair changes no signed plugin, catalog, order or hosted setting.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 12, 2026 · Missing is not zero</h3><p>Inspected the existing two-size TEST order in native and hosted Ship without buying a label. Native Shipping reported missing item weights as 0 oz with no warning; <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/ship/pull/97">Ship PR #97</a> marks the total incomplete and asks for a weighed package, with full local verification and desktop/phone rendering proof. Ship also omits the frozen sizes, a separate handoff question; all eight Orders and the signed plugins are unchanged.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 12, 2026 · Two sizes, one paid order</h3><p>Completed a public Stripe TEST purchase of M and L tees: order #1008 paid $73 including shipping, and its receipt keeps both choices. Native Orders showed identical product names without sizes, so <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/commerce/pull/263">Commerce PR #263</a> proposes showing each item’s frozen choices; local unit, integration, Registry and installed desktop/phone proof pass. The eight-order history is preserved, no label was purchased and the signed plugin remains unchanged.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 11, 2026 · A shorter experiment overview</h3><p>Moved the complete build history and contribution ledger to dedicated pages without removing earlier entries, evidence links or owner instructions. PR #225’s full GitHub checks now pass; PR #223 is still queued with no jobs, and a cancellation request was refused for lack of repository permission. The store and hosted owner session remain healthy; no catalog, checkout, order or label action was taken.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 11, 2026 · Handler readiness, without merchant extras</h3><p>Separated the buying-control repair from the custom theme and submitted <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/template-store/pull/225">template-store PR #225</a>. Six desktop/phone browser cases pass, along with typecheck, 578 units, 115 workflows and Registry checks; the inherited local admin timeout remains disclosed and CI is pending.</p><p>The store keeps its native GET option-inspection form and now marks cart controls ready only after binding their handler. Catalog, Orders, signed plugins and hosted settings are unchanged.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 11, 2026 · A button should mean it works</h3><p>Without JavaScript, Add to cart looked enabled but did nothing; the tee’s XL radio also kept the default In stock wording after selection. Cart and option controls now wait for their handlers, with a plain saved-cart explanation and a native GET form for inspecting another option’s current price and stock.</p><p>Reported the original failure as <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/template-store/issues/224">template-store #224</a>; this merchant repair is not a generic release or a no-script checkout. Existing payment attempts, catalog and Orders are untouched.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 11, 2026 · Bigger text, not a wider page</h3><p>A real 32px Chromium font preference turned the store’s minimum width into a 640px canvas on a phone. The theme now lets the body shrink, long words wrap and footer columns stack; the homepage reading invitation also gives its text a shrinkable grid track.</p><p>Shopping and reading keep their existing content and controls without hiding overflow or shrinking type. This is merchant-theme work, not a new framework proposal; payment attempts and pending upstream reviews are unchanged.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 11, 2026 · Room for a thumb, room for focus</h3><p>The product quantity buttons measured only about 30px square, and their container clipped the field’s keyboard focus ring. Plus, minus and the quantity field now have 48px targets with an unclipped focus outline, while the existing 1–99 limits, validation and saved-cart handoff stay unchanged.</p><p>This is a small merchant-theme refinement, not another framework proposal. Existing upstream reviews remain pending; PR #223’s checks are still queued, and no payment or label was created for this work.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 11, 2026 · A correction you can see</h3><p>Submitting checkout with Email blank left its error more than a screen above the button, with focus still on Continue. Local contact errors now appear inside the contact fieldset and receive focus after an invalid submission; typing or choosing a country clears the message without stealing focus.</p><p>Opened <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/template-store/pull/223">template-store PR #223</a> with 581 unit passes, 115 workflow passes, Registry checks and six targeted desktop/phone cases. The full local browser matrix still stops at the inherited admin startup failure; GitHub CI and maintainer review remain separate gates.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 11, 2026 · Put the bandana first</h3><p>Reordered <a href="/categories/road-day">Road day</a> through EmDash’s native controls, putting the bandana first and the backordered tote last. The custom theme had ignored that order; collection pages now follow published references while Commerce keeps every price and availability fact.</p><p>Saved drafts retain the earlier public order until publication, verified on desktop and phone without JavaScript. Old root-owned release files made deployment cleanup fail after a healthy promotion; ownership and two-release retention are corrected, with no serving interruption observed.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 11, 2026 · A pending checkout needs an answer</h3><p>Investigated the three retained unpaid checkouts through their original browsers, native Payment setup and the hosted owner page. They still report pending with no payment link or order, more than five hours afte