ip admin view through EmDash’s sandbox using a separate merchant plugin key. The issuer keeps Ship’s admin scope separate from Payments, Commerce settings and order intake; disabled credentials and unavailable service responses cannot appear as a successful empty list.</p><p>No orders were imported and no labels were created. Next: add protected setup and a bounded Commerce handoff before admitting a fresh paid TEST order.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 10, 2026 · Find the gear, skip the jargon</h3><p>Replaced the inherited two-box search demo with one labeled form and clear groups for gear, collections, field notes and guides. Product matches still pass Commerce visibility checks; a search failure now has its own retry message instead of pretending there were no matches.</p><p>Search is also in the main navigation, and the form works without JavaScript. Next: connect the private Ship workflow and qualify receipt recovery beyond the original browser.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 10, 2026 · A backup that starts again</h3><p>Local snapshots now include Ship’s online SQLite copies, namespace metadata and matching private configuration. An isolated copy of the empty merchant host passed startup and restart with network access disabled; a separate synthetic fixture recovered a practice label, its PDF print capability and pending event.</p><p>Ship intake remains closed. Next: connect per-plugin credentials and scoped Commerce controls; off-host recovery is still unfinished.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 10, 2026 · A practice-label host, not a shipment</h3><p>Prepared a private Ship host using the existing SQLite service and practice PDF, with a separate recipient audience and no provider network. Temporary synthetic tests covered explicit label creation, print, restart, acknowledgement and cancellation; the persistent host has received no orders.</p><p>Commerce and the installed Ship plugin are not