ping Block Kit sections, instead of one collapsed paragraph. Found while correcting an existing TEST order; no payment, address authority or shipping behavior changes. Node 24.22.0 typecheck, 848 unit/workflow tests, 111 integration tests, audits and official Registry packaging pass; the backend is 129,309 bytes with 1,763 bytes headroom. Installed desktop/phone checks pass with a bounded local Node heap. GitHub’s full checks passed at this head; maintainer review is pending. Not deployed or released, and signed Commerce 0.8.0 is unchanged.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://github.com/saarius/template-store/tree/fix/cart-return-facts">saarius/template-store · fix/cart-return-facts</a></td><td><a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/template-store/pull/220">PR #220</a> at <a href="https://github.com/saarius/template-store/commit/d8cde3a">d8cde3a</a> for <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/template-store/issues/219">issue #219</a>. Refreshes Commerce facts on focus/BFCache return even when saved intent is unchanged, without moving correctly placed rows or resetting failed-write memory and active checkout protection. Equivalent behavior is dogfooded here. Node 24 typecheck, 579 unit tests, 115 workflows (two skips), audits, Registry build and credential-free dry-run pass; four focused cart/checkout desktop/phone cases pass. The full local matrix stops at the unchanged admin welcome observer, also reproduced on untouched main. GitHub’s full desktop, phone, Registry and aggregate checks passed at this head on November 11; maintainer review is pending.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://github.com/saarius/ship/tree/fix/label-history-phone">saarius/ship · fix/label-history-phone</a></td><td><a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/ship/pull/96">PR #96</a> at <a href="https://github.com/saarius/ship/commit/cb23232">cb23232</a> repairs <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/ship/issues/95">issue #95</a>. The hosted page still expands from 390px to 547px; the local renderer now fits 320/390/600/601/1440px with full tracking, named fields, table semantics and keyboard-reachable print/cancel controls. Existing, older/cancelled, practice and long-field histories pass intercepted Chromium checks. Node 24.22.2 full verification passes: 67 plugin/repository tests, 88 Workers tests, typechecks, 26,012-byte Registry backend, dry release/builds and isolated entry proofs. Dispatch checks pass; substantive CI is approval-gated. Not deployed to the shared service; no real order or label was changed.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://github.com/saarius/template-store/tree/fix/cart-fallback-labels">saarius/template-store · fix/cart-fallback-labels</a></td><td><a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/template-store/pull/218">PR #218</a> at <a href="https://github.com/saarius/template-store/commit/3285ebc">3285ebc</a>, open for <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/template-store/issues/217">issue #217</a>. The merchant theme already uses the same fallback-name rule. Node 24.22.0 typecheck, 587 unit tests, 115 workflow tests (two skips), audits, Registry compilation and Wrangler dry-run pass. Four rendered desktop/phone cases cover cart and checkout, unknown/missing/unlisted responses, current-name recovery, distinct accessible controls and exact-ID removal. Browser-local responses are presentation proof, not a payment or real outage. GitHub’s full desktop, phone, Registry and aggregate checks pass at this head; review is pending. The unrelated local admin timeout also occurs on untouched upstream and is disclosed in the PR.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://github.com/saarius/template-store/tree/fix/variant-card-availability">saarius/template-store · fix/variant-card-availability</a></td><td><a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/template-store/pull/216">PR #216</a> at <a href="https://github.com/saarius/template-store/commit/5845563">5845563</a>, open for <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/template-store/issues/215">issue #215</a>. The shared presentation repair is dogfooded in the merchant theme. Node 24.22.0 typecheck, 587 unit tests, 115 workflow tests (two skips), audits and credential-free Registry compilation pass. Fresh paired Registry desktop/phone checks prove the default sold-out and sibling buyable case, selected-size refusal and cart behavior. GitHub’s full desktop, phone, Registry and aggregate checks pass at this head; review is pending. Unrelated local baseline admin timeouts remain documented, not called passes.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://github.com/saarius/ship/tree/fix/settings-box-label">saarius/ship · fix/settings-box-label</a></td><td><a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/ship/pull/94">PR #94</a> at b075e63. Hosted Ship used the same HTML ID for ship-from Name and Box name, so label-based entry changed the wrong field. The merchant saved packing by selecting the box field directly. The fix keeps POST names unchanged; all 67 plugin/repository and 87 Workers tests, typechecks, Registry size, dry builds and isolated entry checks pass, with targeted desktop/phone label and submission proof. CI is awaiting maintainer approval; only dispatch checks have run. Not deployed; shared-service deployment remains the maintainer’s step.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://github.com/saarius/template-store/tree/fix/selected-variant-jsonld">saarius/template-store · fix/selected-variant-jsonld</a></td><td><a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/template-store/pull/214">PR #214</a> at <a href="https://github.com/saarius/template-store/commit/f4c6174">f4c6174</a>, open with green CI. Metadata behavior is dogfooded here: no borrowed identifiers; older member payloads produce page facts without an Offer. The theme’s later visible-identifier repair is merchant-only, not part of this PR. New public member SKUs enable their own Offer in disposable paired-runtime checks. Node 24.22.0 typecheck, 591 unit and 118 workflow tests, targeted desktop/phone checks on both payload generations and the credential-free Registry build pass. After correcting stale policy-test expectations, GitHub’s full desktop, phone and aggregate checks pass at this head; the longer local admin/policy rerun still crashes before those assertions.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://github.com/saarius/commerce/tree/fix/public-variant-sku">saarius/commerce · fix/public-variant-sku</a></td><td><a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/commerce/pull/260">PR #260</a> at <a href="https://github.com/saarius/commerce/commit/73d8523">73d8523</a>, open with green CI. Adds each projected member’s own current SKU without writes or guessed identity. Full local unit/workflow and integration suites, typecheck, audits, Registry size validation and targeted SDK/workerd/SQLite desktop/phone proof pass. The backend is 129,357 bytes, with 1,715 bytes of Registry headroom. No production plugin replacement is deployed; template PR #214 consumes the optional field and safely handles older payloads.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://github.com/saarius/template-store/tree/fix/invalid-cart-quantity">saarius/template-store · fix/invalid-cart-quantity</a></td><td>Submitted as <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/template-store/pull/212">PR #212</a> at <a href="https://github.com/saarius/template-store/commit/823085f">823085f</a> for #211; open, unmerged, CI green. Restores invalid edits without another state store or changes to Commerce. The browser regression uses synthetic catalog/checkout transport. Local typecheck, unit/workflow, targeted browser checks and credential-free Registry compilation passed. GitHub Actions also passed desktop, phone, Registry and aggregate verification; unrelated local baseline timeouts are documented in the PR. This differs from the merchant’s deployed retained-draft repair.</td></tr></tbody></table><table><caption>Store source and legacy work</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Source</th><th scope="col">Status & purpose</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href="https://github.com/saarius/template-store/tree/backroadbum/store">saarius/template-store · backroadbum/store</a></td><td>Branded storefront and public TEST checkout, durable request limits and non-creating readiness telemetry. Local Ship recovery now has online SQLite copies and an isolated restart drill. Visible product identifiers now follow the selected member’s optional public SKU and omit unknown identifiers rather than displaying a sibling’s; simple-product identifiers are unchanged. Store-specific work, not an upstream proposal.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://github.com/saarius/payments/tree/backroadbum/test-runtime">saarius/payments · backroadbum/test-runtime</a></td><td>Retired Node host using v0.5.0 service ports, signed own-account events and durable wakes; service stopped/disabled and its old TEST webhook disabled. Data retained for recovery, not serving hosted Payments. Its merchant issuer gives Ship a separate admin-only grant and Commerce a distinct one-order machine grant only while durable admission is enabled; production admission is disabled. Merchant-only composition, not an upstream release.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://github.com/saarius/commerce/tree/backroadbum/merchant-profile">saarius/commerce · backroadbum/merchant-profile</a></td><td>Legacy merchant-only TEST sandbox build based on v0.8.0, 35f80f218776; no longer mounted during Registry migration. Exact-host transport and local receipt adaptations, plus a merchant-v2 single-order sender with current/disable checks, versioned completion/ACK and protected native Ship links. Disposable sandbox composition is verified; production remains unselected. No upstream proposal. The recorded upstream mode decision keeps mode out of the shopper view, so the local TEST marker is not being submitted as a routine bug fix; full generic verification remains incomplete.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://github.com/saarius/ship/tree/backroadbum/practice-host">saarius/ship · backroadbum/practice-host</a></td><td>Retired private Node/workerd host and merchant admin profile; service stopped/disabled and public routes closed. Signed Registry Ship replaces the custom plugin mount. Host/profile <a href="https://github.com/saarius/ship/commit/a5681bc">a5681bc</a> adds protected native single-order practice-label/PDF actions with version checks, duplicate protection and disabled-state recovery. Admission remains loopback-only, production unselected and closed. No provider network; production intake stays closed. Disposable sender/host composition and native-renderer proof are not merchant fulfillment; no upstream proposal.</td></tr><tr><td>Payments v0.5.0 / Ship v0.3.1</td><td>Signed Registry Payments v0.5.0, Ship v0.3.1 and Commerce v0.8.0 installed through EmDash. Build-time overrides are removed; Commerce and Payments completed hosted consent. Fresh native Payments checks and a hosted TEST purchase are verified; Ship is connected with verified hosted sandbox labels. Local transports are stopped/disabled; their fixture proofs are historical, not hosted fulfillment.</td></tr></tbody></table></section>}
